---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Quiet Grid Press">
  <section class="legal-page">
    <div class="shell legal-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your Information Deserves Respect</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="effective">Effective August 16, 2026</p>

      <h2>Our Starting Point</h2>
      <p>
        Your information is yours. When you choose to share it, we treat that
        choice as a gift of trust and use only what is needed for the purpose
        explained to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Information Collected by This Website</h2>
      <p>
        When you sign up for email updates, we collect the email address you
        provide. Our hosting provider, Netlify, processes the form submission
        so we can securely receive and manage it. The provider may also process
        ordinary technical request information, such as the requested page,
        date and time, browser information, and internet address, as needed to
        deliver and protect the website.
      </p>

      <h2>Email Updates</h2>
      <p>
        We use email addresses submitted through this website only to share
        Quiet Grid Press news, including new-book announcements, puzzle news,
        and occasional offers. We retain an address only as long as needed for
        these updates or necessary recordkeeping. We do not sell or rent email
        addresses.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Quiet Grid Press does not currently use advertising trackers, visitor
        profiles, or browser cookies for analytics. Before additional
        measurement is introduced, this policy will identify what is measured,
        its purpose, its retention, and any available choices.
      </p>

      <h2>Retail Links</h2>
      <p>
        This website links to Amazon so readers can view current book prices and
        availability. When you follow a retail link, Amazon receives the
        information ordinarily associated with visiting its website and handles
        it under Amazon's own privacy practices. Quiet Grid Press does not
        receive your Amazon account or order information through this website.
      </p>

      <h2>What Will Not Change</h2>
      <p>
        Quiet Grid Press will not sell or rent your personal information. We
        will not quietly turn information entrusted to us for one purpose into
        an unrelated product or advertising list.
      </p>

      <h2>Policy Updates</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated as Quiet Grid Press adds carefully reviewed
        services or as legal requirements change. The effective date will
        always appear near the top of this page. Material changes will be
        explained before they take effect whenever practical. An update will
        not change the promise that personal information will not be sold or
        rented.
      </p>

      <h2>Email Choices</h2>
      <p>
        Every marketing email will include a clear, easy way to unsubscribe.
        An unsubscribe request will be recorded only as needed to honor the
        request and prevent future marketing messages unless the person chooses
        to subscribe again.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and Requests</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions may be sent using the postal information on the
        <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
